Z||000008||btoth||09-21-2001||10:11 AM|||| <A HREF="http://emuxhaven.metage.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://emuxhaven.metage.net/</A> <P>For SNES I use Snes9x v1.38<BR>For NES I use NESten - best emulator I've found for Windows.<BR>I did have a playstation emulator that was working - I forget the name now, but I still think Super Mario World is the best game ever made!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (That and the 1st and 3rd Zelda games.)<P>ROMs for the older game systems are very easy to find.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||btoth||09-21-2001||10:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>   anyone know of a way to use your joysticks? And what are the buttons to hit for a and b on a nintendo joystick. ctrl is a but I can't figure out b. I'm like a kid in a candy store...this Rocks!!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just download an emulator that supports DirectInput and then you can go into the setup and just push the buttons on your controller/joystick to set 'em up any way you want.  The emulators I listed do this.<p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 09-21-2001).]||||reg||1
