Z||000012||Sour Lemon||09-22-2001||08:36 PM||||You all think that emulators for the computer are cool...check out the emulators that run ON dreamcast.   <A HREF="http://www.dcemulation.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dcemulation.com/</A> <BR>The NES emu for dreamcast runs really well and is very playable.  <BR>The SNES could use some speed.<BR>The gameboy one is pretty neat.  I'd rather keep my gameboy heh.<BR>I think it's really cool that I can burn a cd and have over 300 games to choose from.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smalside.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000013||btoth||09-24-2001||10:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sour Lemon:<BR><B>You all think that emulators for the computer are cool...check out the emulators that run ON dreamcast.   <A HREF="http://www.dcemulation.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dcemulation.com/</A> <BR>The NES emu for dreamcast runs really well and is very playable.  <BR>The SNES could use some speed.<BR>The gameboy one is pretty neat.  I'd rather keep my gameboy heh.<BR>I think it's really cool that I can burn a cd and have over 300 games to choose from.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Seems silly to go buy a new console system to play old console games when you can just play them on the computer.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  J/K||||reg||1
